Jihad Browser — Licensing Overview
==================================

Jihad Browser is a composite work that incorporates source code from several
upstream projects, each retaining its own license. There is no single license
that covers the entire repository. Every source file retains the license header
of its origin; this file explains how the pieces fit together.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Component licenses
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. User-interface shell (directory: app/)
   Derived from isis-browser (Enyo web app).
   Copyright (c) 2012 Hewlett-Packard Development Company, L.P.
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   Full text: licenses/Apache-2.0.txt

2. Render daemon / IPC layer (directory: render/browserserver/)
   Derived from the isis-project BrowserServer / BrowserAdapter / AdapterBase.
   Copyright (c) 2012 Hewlett-Packard Development Company, L.P.
   Copyright (c) 2012-2014 LG Electronics, Inc.
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   Full text: licenses/Apache-2.0.txt

3. Goanna rendering backend integration (directory: render/goanna/)
   New code authored for Jihad Browser that links against the UXP / Goanna
   engine. Licensed under the Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0, to remain
   compatible with the engine it embeds.
   Full text: licenses/MPL-2.0.txt

4. UXP / Goanna web engine (referenced as an external dependency; NOT vendored
   in this repository — built from the upstream UXP source tree).
   Copyright (c) Mozilla Foundation and the Moonchild Productions / Pale Moon
   contributors.
   Licensed under the Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0, with portions under
   other compatible licenses as documented in the UXP tree.
   Full text: licenses/MPL-2.0.txt

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
License compatibility
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Apache License 2.0 and the Mozilla Public License 2.0 are compatible. The
MPL-2.0 is a file-level (weak) copyleft: MPL-licensed files remain under the MPL
and their source must be made available, but they may be combined with files
under other licenses (including Apache-2.0) in a "Larger Work". See MPL-2.0
section 1.7 and 3.3.

New code added by the Jihad Browser project:
  - Files placed under app/ or render/browserserver/ that are derivative of the
    Apache-2.0 upstreams remain Apache-2.0.
  - Files under render/goanna/ that integrate with the Goanna engine are
    MPL-2.0.
  - Build/packaging glue (build/) is Apache-2.0 unless a file header states
    otherwise.

